<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nabeshima Naomasa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1815–1871</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Nabeshima Kanso</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nabeshima Naomasa was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> of the Saga domain in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a> from 1830 to 1861. Responsible for guarding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagasaki">Nagasaki</a>, he promoted Western learning, built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s first reverberatory furnace in 1850 and cast iron <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a>, giving Saga some of the most modern weapons in Japan. These helped the imperial side in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boshin-war">Boshin War</a> of 1868, and Saga men played a leading part in the Meiji government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nabeshima-naomasa.jpg" alt="Nabeshima Naomasa" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 川崎道民 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nabeshima_Naomasa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
